\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Welcome, happy morning! 
\par Age to age shall say:
\par Hell to-day is vanquished; 
\par Heaven is won to-day!
\par Lo! the dead is living, God for evermore!
\par Him, their true Creator, 
\par All His works adore.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Welcome, Happy Morning! 
\par Age to age shall say.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Earth with joy confesses, 
\par Clothing her for spring,
\par All good gifts returned 
\par with her returning King;
\par Bloom in every meadow,
\par leaves on every bough,
\par Speak His sorrows ended, 
\par hail His triumph now.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Welcome, Happy Morning! 
\par Age to age shall say.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Thou, of life the Author, 
\par death didst undergo,
\par Tread the path of darkness,
\par saving strength to show;
\par Come, then, True and Faithful,
\par now fulfil Thy word;
\par 'Tis Thine own third morning:
\par Rise, O buried Lord!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Welcome, Happy Morning! 
\par Age to age shall say.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Loose the souls long prisoned,
\par bound with Satan's chain;
\par All that now is fallen raise to life again;
\par Show Thy face in brightness, 
\par bid the nations see;
\par Bring again our daylight; 
\par day returns with Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Welcome, Happy Morning! 
\par Age to age shall say.
\par \f1 
